          "emoji": "🧹"
         },
         {
          "title": "Say sorry and be still",
          "body_md": "Khamasamana → Iriyavahiyam → Tassa Uttari → Annattha → kayotsarg (silent Logassa to “chandesu nimmalayara”, or four Navkar) → “Namo Arihantanam” → Logassa aloud.",
          "emoji": "🙇"
         },
         {
          "title": "Check the muhapatti",
          "body_md": "Khamasamana, ask permission (*“Samayik muhapatti padilehu?”*, then *“Ichchham”*), then do *muhapatti padilehan*: open it, look carefully so no tiny being is trapped, and fold it back while reflecting on the *bol*: 50 in all, and girls and women usually say 40 of them. Your teacher will teach these.",
          "emoji": "😷"
         }
        ],
        "review": "needs_pathshala_review"
